N5008 [temp.variadic]/4-5.  A NON-type parameter pack expanded as CALL ARGUMENTS
(`add(I...)`) expands to one argument per element, in a function-template body
and inside a `decltype` return type.  Previously the pack's element values were
not substituted, so `add(I...)` produced a nondeterministic result; fixed by
expanding a non-type call-argument pack from pack_expr_map in both
expand_call_argument_packs and the function-template body.  The explicitly-
argumented core of std::apply's `__invoke(f, get<I>(t)...)`.  Non-vacuous: each
assertion would read a nondeterministic value under the old behaviour.
